# TypeScript — Infrastructure (Strict)

Apply to **new or modified** code in scoped files. Do not mass-refactor untouched legacy `any`.

## Required

| Rule | Rationale |
|------|-----------|
| **No new `any` or `as any`** | Use `unknown` + narrowing, generics, or a named interface. Exception: unavoidable third-party gaps — add a one-line comment explaining why. |
| **Redux: `RootState` / `AppDispatch`** | `useSelector((state: RootState) => ...)` and `useDispatch<AppDispatch>()` — never `state: any` in new code. |
| **No bare `Function` type** | Use explicit signatures: `(value: string) => void`, not `onChange?: Function`. |
| **Explicit return types on exports** | All exported functions, hooks, and service methods declare return type (`: Promise<T>`, `: UseXReturn`, `: void`). |
| **Axios interceptors typed** | Use `InternalAxiosRequestConfig` / `AxiosResponse` from `axios`, not `request: any`. |
| **API payloads as interfaces** | Define `*Request` / `*Response` interfaces in the same file or colocated `*.types.ts` — avoid `requestBody: any` on new endpoints. |
| **`interface` vs `type`** | `interface` for object shapes and extendable props; `type` for unions, literals, and aliases. |
| **Prefer `readonly` on config objects** | Immutable config/constants use `as const` or `readonly` fields where the codebase already does. |

## Examples

```typescript
// Redux — required in new/modified hooks/components using store
import { RootState, AppDispatch } from "../../Config/store";

const actorId = useSelector((state: RootState) => state.loginDetails.actorId);
const dispatch = useDispatch<AppDispatch>();

// Hook return type — required on export
interface UseApiReturn {
  isLoading: boolean;
  error: unknown;
  doGet: (url: string) => Promise<ApiResponse>;
  doPost: (url: string, body: Record<string, unknown>, headers?: RequestHeaders) => Promise<ApiResponse>;
}
const useApi = (): UseApiReturn => { ... };

// Helper — no any
export const getRequestBodyHeaders = (
  functionCode: string,
  functionSubCode: string,
): RequestHeaders => { ... };

// Interceptor
import type { InternalAxiosRequestConfig } from "axios";

const interceptor = async (config: InternalAxiosRequestConfig): Promise<InternalAxiosRequestConfig> => { ... };
```

## Legacy touch-only paths

If a file is edited for a one-line bugfix unrelated to types, do not refactor the whole file to remove existing `any`.
